{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"db5f69f9e54fc4e1","type":"text","text":"## Os Discovery / Banner Grabbing","x":-409,"y":-117,"width":370,"height":60},
		{"id":"bddddb2dad742b81","type":"text","text":"Banner grabbing or OS Fingerprinting is the method used to `determine the operating system running on a remote target system`","x":100,"y":-138,"width":356,"height":103},
		{"id":"c7e88faab633ab0e","type":"text","text":"Active Banner Grabbing","x":660,"y":-260,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"5f107eeb56e9cf75","type":"text","text":"Passive Banner Grabbing","x":665,"y":20,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"7c4b27e73ccc4657","type":"text","text":"There are two methods of banner grabbing spoiting the banner while trying to connect to a service such as `FTP site ` and downlaoding the binary `file/bin/ls` to check the system architecture.","x":37,"y":-700,"width":483,"height":129},
		{"id":"77aba2c865369606","type":"text","text":"In Active Banner grabbing - Attacker send a variety of malformed packet to the remote host and response are compared with database\n```\nResponse from diffrent OS vary beacause of diffrences in TCP/IP stack implementation\n```","x":1040,"y":-320,"width":567,"height":180},
		{"id":"81d57b8ca86832f1","type":"file","file":"Cyber Security Practically/screenshots/nine_steps_of_banner_grabbing.png","x":1720,"y":-370,"width":400,"height":281},
		{"id":"ae37903c725041e5","type":"text","text":"**Active Banner Grabbing** me attacker/scanner **directly target server se communicate karta hai** aur response me banner collect karta hai.","x":504,"y":-473,"width":563,"height":78},
		{"id":"5e4a2096c0212c94","type":"text","text":"Nmap\nNetcat\nTelnet\nOpenSSL\ncurl\nwget","x":1274,"y":-520,"width":100,"height":167},
		{"id":"8a8eb6a594533b64","type":"text","text":"Passive Fingerprinting capture packets from the target host via sniffing to study telltale signs that can reveal an OS","x":1040,"y":20,"width":567,"height":60},
		{"id":"4e0c20e7bf417234","type":"text","text":"**Passive Banner Grabbing** me attacker **target ko koi request nahi bhejta**. Sirf network traffic observe karke banner ya service information collect karta hai.","x":1040,"y":-118,"width":567,"height":100},
		{"id":"eb2dd065554a1cb6","type":"text","text":"Sniffing the network traffics","x":1199,"y":340,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"03dfb4f6a751b4c1","type":"text","text":"Banner grabbing from error messages","x":900,"y":340,"width":212,"height":60},
		{"id":"0e0a2bd249c1b798","type":"text","text":"Banner Grabbing from page extentions","x":1540,"y":340,"width":215,"height":60},
		{"id":"22059f7e2600c5e4","type":"text","text":"Error messages provide information such as : \n- Types of server\n- Types of Os\n- SSL tools used by target remote system","x":900,"y":520,"width":212,"height":220},
		{"id":"594d1b210606c459","type":"text","text":"Capturing and analyzing packets from the target enable an attacker to determine the OS used by the remote host","x":1199,"y":520,"width":250,"height":140},
		{"id":"1a2b37e7817972f2","type":"text","text":"Looking for an extension in the url may help in determining the application version. For Example .aspx = IIS server and Windows Plateform","x":1540,"y":500,"width":215,"height":220},
		{"id":"f41bd6b36d23cac2","type":"text","text":"There are `four Areas` that typically determine the OS are given below","x":900,"y":960,"width":855,"height":60},
		{"id":"ec5676beaa63f3ea","type":"text","text":"```\nTTL = Time To Live\nTOS = Type of service\nDF  = Default Fragment\n```\n\n\n```\nTTL of the packets: What does the OS sets as the TTL on the outbound packets.\n\nWindow size : What is the window size sets by the OS.\n\nWeather the DF bit is set: Does the os set the DF bit.\n\nTOS : Does the os set the TOS. and if so what setting it is.\n```","x":900,"y":1120,"width":855,"height":360},
		{"id":"29ff1e5b0a3df651","type":"text","text":"**TTL** IP header ka ek field hai jo batata hai ki **ek packet network me maximum kitne routers (hops) cross kar sakta hai**. Har router TTL ko **1 se kam** karta hai. Agar TTL **0** ho jaye to packet drop kar diya jata hai.\n```\nPC -------- Router1 -------- Router2 -------- Server\n\nTTL = 64\n```\n\nisme TTL value 64 hai ab ye 65 router se hokar jayega jaise hi TTL ki value -1 hogi ye packet drop kar dega","x":900,"y":1500,"width":855,"height":400},
		{"id":"d523301f9bc43c60","type":"text","text":"|Operating System|TTL|\n|---|--:|\n|Linux|64|\n|Windows|128|\n|Cisco|255","x":1840,"y":1500,"width":254,"height":151},
		{"id":"a27600b6bdaefa96","type":"text","text":"### DF (Don't Fragment)\n\n#### Definition\n\n**DF (Don't Fragment)** IPv4 header ka ek flag hai jo batata hai ki **packet ko network me fragment (tukdo me divide) nahi kiya ja sakta**.","x":-60,"y":1204,"width":420,"height":193},
		{"id":"ebaf9004b4905d1e","type":"text","text":"TCP Window Size\n\n## Definition\n\n**TCP Window Size** TCP header ka ek field hai jo batata hai ki **receiver ek baar me kitna data receive kar sakta hai bina ACK bheje**.\n\nYe **Flow Control** ke liye use hota hai.\n\n---\n\n## Why use Window Size?\n\n- Data overflow rokne ke liye.\n- Sender ki speed control karne ke liye.\n- Network performance improve karne ke liye.","x":-60,"y":1485,"width":420,"height":435},
		{"id":"5d2f871449fa4c3e","type":"text","text":"# ToS (Type of Service)\n\n## Definition\n\n**ToS (Type of Service)** IPv4 header ka ek field hai jo packet ki **priority aur handling preference** batata hai.\n\nModern networks me ise **DSCP (Differentiated Services Code Point)** aur **ECN** ne largely replace kar diya hai.\n\n---\n\n## Why use ToS?\n\n- Voice traffic ko priority dene ke liye.\n- Video streaming optimize karne ke liye.\n- QoS (Quality of Service) implement karne ke liye.","x":-60,"y":740,"width":500,"height":430},
		{"id":"b118e36b9bde3751","type":"text","text":"| Field       | Full Form       | Work                                        |\n| ----------- | --------------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| TTL         | Time To Live    | Packet kitne hops tak ja sakta hai          |\n| DF          | Don't Fragment  | Packet ko fragment hone se rokta hai        |\n| Window Size | TCP Window Size | Receiver ek baar me kitna data le sakta hai |\n| ToS         | Type of Service | Packet ki priority/QoS define karta hai     |\n","x":-60,"y":500,"width":620,"height":180},
		{"id":"b704f5842b3c76cc","type":"text","text":"#### Why Banner Grabbing ?\nDetermine system vulnerability and exploit that ","x":-1080,"y":-136,"width":395,"height":99},
		{"id":"dbd00b25808f7ae0","type":"text","text":"### How attacker identify target os","x":2570,"y":-182,"width":350,"height":60},
		{"id":"74f6bdf56c29e85c","type":"text","text":"Attackers can identify the OS running on the target machine by looking at the `TTL` and `TCP Window size` in the IP header of the first packet in a TCP session","x":3020,"y":-203,"width":460,"height":102},
		{"id":"9bfa7be48408a72f","type":"text","text":"| Operating System | Default TTL | Typical TCP Window Size |\n| ---------------- | ----------: | ----------------------: |\n| Windows XP       |         128 |                   65535 |\n| Windows 7        |         128 |    8192 (commonly seen) |\n| Windows 10       |         128 |   Dynamic (Auto-Tuning) |\n| Windows 11       |         128 |   Dynamic (Auto-Tuning) |\n| Linux (older)    |          64 |                    5840 |\n| Linux (modern)   |          64 |   Dynamic (e.g. 29200+) |\n| Ubuntu           |          64 |                 Dynamic |\n| Debian           |          64 |                 Dynamic |\n| Kali Linux       |          64 |                 Dynamic |\n| macOS            |          64 |                 Dynamic |\n| FreeBSD          |          64 |                   65535 |\n| OpenBSD          |          64 |                   16384 |\n| Cisco IOS        |         255 |                  Varies |\n","x":3300,"y":0,"width":517,"height":420},
		{"id":"a9f332ffc71b76c3","type":"text","text":"Tools\n- Nmap \n- Wireshark\n- UnicornScan\n- Nmap Script engine\n- Nmap : IPv6 fingerprinting","x":3300,"y":560,"width":517,"height":206}
	],
